-- title:
--   Surjectivity of Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation at tower level ℓ
-- statement:
--   The theorem concerns a fixed prime $\ell$ of the Hecke tower away from two primes $r\neq\bar r$, and asserts that the $\pi$-adic uniformisation maps at level $\ell$ hit every geometric point. The hypotheses fall into the following groups.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r\neq r$, and a nonzero natural number $N$ which is squarefree and divisible by neither $r$ nor $\bar r$.
--
--   **Coefficient ring.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), in which the images of $2$ and of $3$ are units (`h2`, `h3`), together with an irreducible element $\pi$ such that $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete, $\operatorname{card}(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$, and $(r)=(\pi)$; and a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is a fraction field of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Unramified covering ring.** A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra, together with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, such that $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal is maximal, every element of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfies a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $F_r(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`).
--
--   **Determinant valuation.** A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) characterised by `hvdet`: $\mathrm{vdet}(g)=n$ exactly when $\det g=u\,\pi^{n}$ in $K_0$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and coarse moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ with `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`, i.e. $0<a$ or $0<b$, and for every height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ the completion $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb Q}\mathbb Q_v$ is a division algebra precisely when $v$ divides $r$ or $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda$ (an order not properly contained in any order); a scheme $\mathcal X$ with a morphism $f$ to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and a family `pt` of $\mathcal O$-points attached to fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure, satisfying `IsCoarseModuli Λ N 𝒳 f pt` (invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on points over algebraically closed fields up to isomorphism, and the universal property among such families); the generic fibre of $f$ over $K_0$, realised as the second pullback projection, is geometrically reduced and geometrically connected.
--
--   **Auxiliary full level and fine moduli.** An integer $n\ge 3$ prime to $r$, to $\bar r$ and to $N$; a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a family `ptF` on fake elliptic curves with full level-$n$ structure satisfying `IsFineModuli Λ N n M fM ptF`; a group $G$ with $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ and labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ satisfying `IsLevelTwistAction` (each $\rho h$ lies over the base, twisting a full level structure by $\chi h$ transports moduli points along $\rho h$, and $\chi$ is multiplicative, injective and surjective modulo $n$).
--
--   **Forgetful and degeneracy structure.** A morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ with $p$ followed by $f$ equal to $f_M$, invariant under $\rho$, and compatible with the two families of moduli points (`hp_pt`). For every prime $\ell'$ of the tower away from $r,\bar r$, a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_{\ell'}$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ for fake elliptic curves with extra level $\ell'$ (`IsCoarseModuliT`), with geometrically reduced and geometrically connected fibre over $K_0$, and two degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_{\ell'}\to\mathcal X$ over the base, $d_0$ forgetting the extra level and $d_1$ recording the target of an $\ell'$-level isogeny (`hd₀`, `hd₁`). Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}\colon\mathcal X\to\mathcal X$ over the base, sending the moduli point of $E$ to that of $E'$ whenever $E'$ is the Atkin–Lehner quotient of $E$ at $r$, respectively at $\bar r$.
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with `IsDefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt rbar`, i.e. $a_1<0$, $b_1<0$ and the local algebra is a division algebra exactly at the place above $\bar r$; a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ and an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ with $R_1\le\Lambda_1$; an adelic unit $n_1$ in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` such that $R_1\cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$; an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\iota_0\colon\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$; a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$; and the subgroup $\tilde\Gamma=\Gamma t$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^{\times}$ characterised as the units lying in the local unit boxes of $R_1$ at all places other than $v$.
--
--   **Hecke elements of the tower.** Families $s$ and $s_f$ indexed by the tower primes, where `hs` requires, for each $\ell'$: the component of $s_f(\ell')$ at each finite place not above $r$ is $s(\ell')\otimes 1$, its component at places above $r$ is $1$, the product of the diagonal idele of the scalar $\ell'$ with $s_f(\ell')^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ'` when $\ell'\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ'` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s(\ell'))=\ell'$; together with the subgroups $\tilde\Gamma(\ell')=\tilde\Gamma\cap s(\ell')\tilde\Gamma s(\ell')^{-1}$. Further, a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\tilde\Gamma$.
--
--   **Uniformisation data at levels $M$ and $\mathcal Y$.** A homomorphism $\theta_t\colon\tilde\Gamma\to G$; a family $\Theta_f$ assigning, to each $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent, a map from triples (an $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to B$, a Deligne datum in $(\Omega\,K_0\,\pi)(B)$, an element of $G$) to the $B$-points of $f_M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$; and families $\Theta_T(\ell')$ defined similarly without the $G$-coordinate, with values in the points of $g_{\ell'}$. These satisfy: functoriality (`hnat`, `hnatT`); $G$-equivariance $\rho(h)\circ\Theta_f(x,gh)=\Theta_f(x,g)$ (`hG`); invariance under the twisted action of $\tilde\Gamma$ through $\iota_0$ and $\theta_t$ (`hinv`), and of $\tilde\Gamma(\ell')$ on $\Theta_T$ (`hiT`); formal étaleness over square-zero-type surjections (`het`); the fibre criterion `hfib`, which says that for $k$ an algebraically closed field with $\pi$ nilpotent, $\Theta_f((\psi,P),g)=\Theta_f((\psi',P'),g')$ holds exactly when there is $\gamma\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $g'=\theta_t(\gamma)g$, with $P'$ the pullback of $P$ along $\iota_0(\gamma)^{-1}$, and with $\psi'y=\psi(F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0\gamma)}y)$ for every $y\in\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ fixed by $F_r^{\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 z)}$ for all central $z\in\tilde\Gamma$ with $\theta_t(z)=1$; the analogous fibre criterion `hfibT` for $\Theta_T(\ell')$ with $\tilde\Gamma(\ell')$; surjectivity `hsurj` of $\Theta_f$ on geometric points for each fixed $\psi$; and compatibility `hiv0`: $d_0(\ell')\circ\Theta_T(\ell')(x)=p\circ\Theta_f(x,1)$.
--
--   **The level-$\ell$ package.** A tower prime $\ell$; a scheme $M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a family `ptFℓ` on pairs (full level-$n$ structure, extra level-$\ell$ structure) satisfying `IsFineModuliT Λ N n ℓ Mℓ fMℓ ptFℓ`; morphisms $\pi_\ell\colon M_\ell\to M$ and $p_\ell\colon M_\ell\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over the base, compatible with the moduli points (`hπℓ`, `hpℓ`); an action $\rho_\ell\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M_\ell$ over the base, commuting with $\pi_\ell$ up to $\rho$, leaving $p_\ell$ fixed, and twisting the level-$\ell$ moduli points by $\chi$ (`hρℓtw`). A family $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ with values in the $\pi$-nilpotent points of $f_{M_\ell}$, satisfying functoriality (`hnatℓ`), $G$-equivariance (`hGℓ`), invariance under the twisted action of elements of $\tilde\Gamma\cap\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$ (`hinvℓ`), formal étaleness (`hetℓ`), the fibre criterion (`hfibℓ`), as in `hfib` but with $\gamma$ additionally required to lie in $\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$, and compatibility with the two projections: $\pi_\ell\circ\Theta_{f,\ell}=\Theta_f$ (`hπℓΘ`) and $p_\ell\circ\Theta_{f,\ell}(x,1)=\Theta_T(\ell)(x)$ (`hpℓΘ`).
--
--   **Inputs about level $\ell$.** The morphism $g_\ell$ is geometrically connected (`hZT`); an open subset $V_\ell$ of the space of $M_\ell$ such that, for every point $x$, the conjunction of $x\in V_\ell$ with the existence of an algebraically closed field $k$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and a $k$-point $y$ of $f_{M_\ell}$ carrying the closed point to $x$ is equivalent to the existence of such $k$ and $y$ carrying the closed point to $x$ and lying in the image of $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ (`hVℓ`); an element $w_{\mathrm{odd},\ell}$ of $\tilde\Gamma\cap\tilde\Gamma(\ell)$ with $\mathrm{vdet}(\iota_0 w_{\mathrm{odd},\ell})=1$; and `hne`, the nonemptiness, for every algebraically closed field $k$ which is an $\mathcal O$-algebra with $\pi$ nilpotent, of the set of $\mathcal O$-algebra maps $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$ and of the set of Deligne data over $k$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two statements hold.
--
--   First: for every algebraically closed field $k$ that is an $\mathcal O$-algebra in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\psi\colon\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to k$, and every morphism $y\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to M_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, there exist a Deligne datum $P$ over $k$ and an element $g\in G$ with $\Theta_{f,\ell}((\psi,P),g)=y$.
--
--   Second: for every such $k$ and $\psi$, and every morphism $y\colon\operatorname{Spec}k\to\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, there exists a Deligne datum $P$ over $k$ with $\Theta_T(\ell)(\psi,P)=y$.
--
--   Thus the uniformisation maps are surjective on geometric points of the $\pi$-nilpotent fibres at level $\ell$, for each fixed choice of the coefficient map $\psi$.
--
--   This is the surjectivity step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld $\pi$-adic uniformisation of Shimura curves, transported to the tower level $\ell$: the uniformisation maps $\Theta_{f,\ell}$ and $\Theta_T(\ell)$, constructed from the Bruhat–Tits–Deligne data and the arithmetic group $\tilde\Gamma$ attached to the definite quaternion algebra, reach every geometric point of the fine moduli scheme $M_\ell$ and of the coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$-nilpotents. It feeds the identification of the $\pi$-adic uniformisation of the minus part of the Hecke tower.
